{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David, when he changed his taste</b> — his taste is his heart and his intellect and his knowledge, like 'those who change taste' [1 Samuel 21:14, reading טעם]. And in Achish [he had] two names, and there are many like it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads the psalm heading's בשנותו את טעמו as 'when he changed his taste/understanding,' glossing טעם as inner discernment. The clause ואכיש היו לו שני שמות is rendered hyper-literally; it likely refers to David being called by two names before Achish, but the syntax is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:25.837310990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}